- **Self-Repair (`self-repair`)**: Always read [`.agents/skills/self-repair/SKILL.md`](./.agents/skills/self-repair/SKILL.md) and load [`.agents/autofix.json`](./.agents/autofix.json) at session start and before executing any task. Immediately record any new user correction or preference to `.agents/autofix.json`.
- **Codebase Memory (`codebase-memory`)**: Always follow [`.agents/skills/codebase-memory/SKILL.md`](./.agents/skills/codebase-memory/SKILL.md) (`index_status` / `index_repository` first, then `search_graph`, `trace_path`, `get_code_snippet`) before searching or exploring the codebase.
- **GitHub Triage (`github-triage`)**: Always read and follow [`.agents/skills/github-triage/SKILL.md`](./.agents/skills/github-triage/SKILL.md) whenever fixing any bug or regression — whether autonomously detected during development/testing or explicitly requested by the user. Automatically ensure GitHub issue infrastructure is active, log diagnostic investigation, verify the fix, link the newly formulated imperative rule in `autofix.json` to the GitHub issue (`"Issue": "#N"`), and close the issue upon verification.
